asr-000236
00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:52.430
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: next year's DSWD budget.

asr-000237
00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.430
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Let me move onto the first slide.

asr-000238
00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:56.870
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The Department of Social Welfare

asr-000239
00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:58.230
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and Development including

asr-000240
00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.710
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: its attached and supervised agencies,

asr-000241
00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:01.710
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: is

asr-000242
00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:19.110
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: honored to appear before the House of Representatives as part of our accountability for the budget appropriated by Congress. In the next slides, we will present our annual budget utilization performance with some details on how we made good use of the allotments and then we will present the proposed budget for 2027.

asr-000243
00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:35.270
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The DSWD's budget increased over the years and for this, we are thankful for the support of Congress. In turn, we made sure we put premium on the trust and the channeling our resources towards people-centered investments.

asr-000244
00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:49.070
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: First, human capital development. Reducing and ultimately ending poverty begins with investing in people's capabilities, particularly children, families, senior citizens, persons with disabilities, and other vulnerable sectors.

asr-000245
00:14:49.110 --> 00:15:00.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We continue to innovate developmental interventions to improve the implementation of the different programs of the DSWD. Second, community-driven development. We continue to engage

asr-000246
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:06.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the people in the farthest communities as partners in identifying needs, designing solutions and

asr-000247
00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:11.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: building resiliency. And third, rapid, adequate and sustained disaster response. This is needed

asr-000248
00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:16.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to ensure that the gains in human capital development, particularly in communities of

asr-000249
00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:22.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: vulnerable groups, are not reversed by the severity of disasters. The instruction of the

asr-000250
00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:29.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: president is clear. The government should be there to respond immediately and remain present for as

asr-000251
00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:34.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: long as families need support to recover. The next slides will show our report to Congress on

asr-000252
00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:39.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: how we spent our budget. For our financial performance for fiscal year 2025, the DBM

asr-000253
00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:48.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: released approximately $265 billion to the DSWD, both for our agency budget and releases from other

asr-000254
00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:55.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: fund sources. We are pleased to report that the DSWD achieved a near 100% utilization rate as of

asr-000255
00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:58.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: July 2026. For fiscal year

asr-000256
00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:00.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 2026,

asr-000258
00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:10.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The DSWD has so far utilized 70% of the agency-specific budget of $262.9 billion. For the Calamity Fund and

asr-000259
00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:18.440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Quick Response Fund replenishments, 78% of the $9.6 billion released so far has already been utilized.

asr-000260
00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:26.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The marching order to all DSWD programs is simple. Work harder, work faster and work smarter.

asr-000261
00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We should not waste resources, and every peso

asr-000262
00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:31.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: appropriated to the DSWD

asr-000263
00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:38.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: is a lifeline for beneficiaries in need. By directing our budget towards people centers investments,

asr-000264
00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:44.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we bring our mandate to life, protect people in crises so that it would not become a long-term

asr-000265
00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:49.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: setback, promote human development to improve people's capabilities and opportunities,

asr-000266
00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:50.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Prevent

asr-000267
00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:53.440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: abuse and exploitation of people in

asr-000268
00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:55.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: vulnerable situations. And

asr-000269
00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:58.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: transform people's lives by addressing structural barriers

asr-000270
00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:06.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: that reproduce poverty and exclusion. So in DSWD, these four roles are interconnected

asr-000271
00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:12.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and social protection is the bridge, not the destination. The goal is not simply to help

asr-000272
00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:19.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: people survive today, but government must work to give them a fairer chance to move forward.

asr-000273
00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:25.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: With this implementation track record as a backdrop, we now present the DSWD's

asr-000274
00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:31.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Families Proposed Budget for Fiscal Year 2027. The proposed budget reflects our commitment to

asr-000275
00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:37.680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: building a bridge to self-sufficiency for every vulnerable client being served by the DSWD and

asr-000276
00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:43.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: its attached and supervised agencies. It is designed to sustain critical social protection

asr-000277
00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:48.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and social welfare interventions while strengthening the systems through assistance

asr-000278
00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:55.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: that is targeted, delivered, monitored, and evaluated. For Fiscal Year 2027,

asr-000279
00:17:55.120 --> 00:18:01.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the DSWD has a total budget of $241.2 billion under the National Expenditure Program.

asr-000280
00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:07.700
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Of this amount, $235.7 billion is allocated to the DSWD Office of the Secretary.

asr-000281
00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:14.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For attached agencies, the proposed budgets are as follows. $136.3 million for the Council of

asr-000282
00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:19.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the Welfare of Children, $91.6 million for the National Council on Disability Affairs,

asr-000283
00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:24.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: $126.3 million for the Juvenile Justice and Welfare Council,

asr-000284
00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:25.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: $811.8

asr-000286
00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:29.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: million for the National Authority for Child Care.

asr-000287
00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:35.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For the supervised agencies, the proposed budgets are $3.8 billion for the National Commission on

asr-000288
00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:43.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Senior Citizens, $359.9 million for the National Anti-Poverty Commission, and $233.4 million for

asr-000289
00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:48.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the Presidential Commission for the Urban Poor. Compared with Fiscal Year 2026,

asr-000290
00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:55.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: General Appropriations Act, the proposed budget under the Fiscal Year 2027 NEP for the DSWD includes

asr-000291
00:18:55.100 --> 00:19:03.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: its attached and supervised agencies, reflects lower levels, with the exception of NACC and NCSC,

asr-000292
00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:08.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: whose budget increases are on their personnel services, because of the new positions created

asr-000293
00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:14.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and or filled up. It is also important to note that pursuant to Executive Order 123 issued on

asr-000294
00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:22.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: August 18, 2026, the NAPC and the PCUP have been placed under the administrative supervision of

asr-000295
00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:25.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the Office of the President. Accordingly, while

asr-000296
00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:29.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: their Fiscal Year 2027 budget figures are reflected in this

asr-000297
00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:35.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: presentation, these two agencies are no longer under the administrative supervision of DSWD.

asr-000298
00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:40.240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Looking at the budget by expenditure classification, the bulk of the budget remains

asr-000299
00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:45.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: primarily directed towards delivery of programs and services to our beneficiaries. Generally,

asr-000300
00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:51.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the operating budgets of all the offices for 2027 are lower than 2026. As mentioned,

asr-000301
00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:55.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the increases pertain to the filling up of plantille position, which is very important for the

asr-000302
00:19:55.080 --> 00:20:01.240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: positions authorized by the DBM. Except for the DSWD, which was granted capital outlay for five

asr-000303
00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:06.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: centers and residential care facilities in year three implementation of a learning institute in

asr-000304
00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:14.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Davao and a warehouse in Iliilo, the DSWD has no capital outlay for 2027. We now proceed to the

asr-000305
00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:20.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: major PAPs. We will provide you with their performance and accomplishments and report to

asr-000306
00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:24.700
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the members of this August subcommittee what we're doing to further improve service delivery.

asr-000307
00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:29.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For the protective services for individuals and families in different circumstances,

asr-000308
00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:34.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the bulk of the budget pertains to the assistance to individuals and families in crisis situation

asr-000309
00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:43.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: or AICs. Although there are also community-based protective social welfare programs that we

asr-000310
00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:49.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: implement to different vulnerable and marginalized sectors. For fiscal year 2025, we have already

asr-000311
00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:54.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: utilized 100 percent of the budget which enabled the program to assist more than 9.4 million

asr-000312
00:20:54.920 --> 00:21:01.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: beneficiaries for the year. For 2026, budget utilization is on track at almost 70 percent

asr-000313
00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:10.300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: of the allotment utilizing all its cash programming in real time, serving 4.24 million beneficiaries so

asr-000314
00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:18.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: far. For fiscal year 2027, the proposed allocation is 33.3 billion consisting of 29.4 billion in

asr-000315
00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:24.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: subsidies. Given the demand-driven nature of the program, the NEP amount may not be

asr-000316
00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:30.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: enough to achieve the same level of performance for the past two years. We have informed our

asr-000317
00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:34.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: budget sponsor about this matter and we have included also in our letter to the honorable

asr-000318
00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:39.700
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: chair of the appropriations committee. Mr. Chair, in a bit, when we get into the discussions,

asr-000319
00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:46.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we will show you a presentation that will show the adverse effect of this budget decline for the

asr-000320
00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:52.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: assistance to individuals in crisis situation and the potential displacements of beneficiaries for

asr-000321
00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:54.820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: medical and other social welfare programs.

asr-000322
00:21:54.860 --> 00:22:00.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Your honors, it is given that AICS continues to fulfill its core mandate by providing a

asr-000323
00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:06.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: comprehensive menu of assistance to individuals and families in crisis situations. But beyond

asr-000324
00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:13.040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: individual emergencies, AICS now serves as our primary tool for adaptive and shock responsive

asr-000325
00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:18.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: social protection, allowing us to quickly act in cases of shocks which impact groups,

asr-000326
00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:23.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: families or communities at risk. In response to the national energy emergency declared

asr-000327
00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:24.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: by the president,

asr-000328
00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:32.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: AICS is at the forefront and is in the front and center of the whole of government intervention under the Uplift program.

asr-000329
00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:40.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Through AICS, the government was able to put into motion interventions using three mechanisms under the adaptive and shock-responsive social protection.

asr-000330
00:22:40.920 --> 00:22:45.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: When the government needed to question impact of the Middle East crisis to our transport sector,

asr-000331
00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:54.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the DSWD rolled out the cash relief assistance to drivers affected by the sudden increase in fuel prices as an emergency scheme.

asr-000332
00:22:54.060 --> 00:23:04.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Under this mechanism, we adopted a group-based assessment supported through identification, validation, and endorsement by relevant authorities or partner agencies.

asr-000333
00:23:05.180 --> 00:23:10.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This assistance helped 1.839 million transport workers nationwide.

asr-000334
00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:17.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: A rapid assessment by the SWS Commission by the Australia Spring Programme

asr-000335
00:23:17.060 --> 00:23:22.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: confirms that our cash relief assistance delivered immediate, decisive, impactful, and overwhelming

asr-000336
00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:23.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with

asr-000337
00:23:24.060 --> 00:23:33.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: an overwhelming 96% of transport workers reporting that the 5,000 grant was operationally crucial in keeping them on the road,

asr-000338
00:23:33.420 --> 00:23:38.900
