DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: more innovative livelihood opportunities.

asr-000510
00:37:59.080 --> 00:38:05.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The objective is to move SLP from one-time livelihood assistance to sustained enterprise

asr-000511
00:38:05.800 --> 00:38:10.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: development with government investment linked to viability, market access, and the capacity

asr-000512
00:38:10.900 --> 00:38:13.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: of beneficiaries to compete.

asr-000513
00:38:13.340 --> 00:38:17.820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The department also continues to provide residential and center-based services for individuals

asr-000514
00:38:17.820 --> 00:38:21.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: who require more intense and sustained care.

asr-000515
00:38:21.000 --> 00:38:25.460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This includes children, older persons, people with disabilities, and other individuals

asr-000516
00:38:25.460 --> 00:38:28.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: whose circumstances require specialized intervention.

asr-000517
00:38:28.600 --> 00:38:36.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For fiscal year 2025, we served 9,620 clients, exceeding a target by 11.34%, while in fiscal

asr-000518
00:38:36.480 --> 00:38:43.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: year 2026, 8,067 clients have already been served as of this reporting period.

asr-000519
00:38:43.200 --> 00:38:48.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For fiscal year 2027, we are proposing 3.3 billion to continue these specialized services

asr-000520
00:38:48.220 --> 00:38:50.660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with a target of 8,640 clients.

asr-000521
00:38:51.000 --> 00:38:55.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Our challenge is to ensure that our facilities remain safe, appropriate, accessible, and

asr-000522
00:38:55.960 --> 00:39:00.280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: capable of delivering quality social welfare services.

asr-000523
00:39:00.280 --> 00:39:04.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: While we continue to provide socialized care to clients, we also need to address the capacity

asr-000524
00:39:04.600 --> 00:39:09.940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and infrastructure constraints of our residential care and center-based facilities.

asr-000525
00:39:09.940 --> 00:39:13.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: At present, DSWD manages 77 facilities.

asr-000526
00:39:13.620 --> 00:39:19.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Of these, 11 facilities, or 14.3%, were established 50 years ago.

asr-000527
00:39:19.000 --> 00:39:20.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Or earlier.

asr-000529
00:39:21.000 --> 00:39:22.000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Or earlier.

asr-000530
00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:26.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: While another 35 facilities are already 30 to 49 years old.

asr-000531
00:39:26.400 --> 00:39:30.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This highlights the need to continuously invest in the facilities where our clients receive

asr-000532
00:39:30.980 --> 00:39:31.980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: care.

asr-000533
00:39:31.980 --> 00:39:36.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We are therefore pursuing facilities upgrading and service expansion.

asr-000534
00:39:36.920 --> 00:39:41.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: At the same time, we are implementing a cost-of-care subsidy for registered licensed and accredited

asr-000535
00:39:41.840 --> 00:39:46.060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: private residential-based social welfare agencies.

asr-000536
00:39:46.060 --> 00:39:50.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This allows us to expand the capacity of the social welfare system by working with qualified

asr-000537
00:39:50.760 --> 00:39:57.820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: partners while continuing to support the regular upkeep and improvement of DSWD facilities.

asr-000538
00:39:57.820 --> 00:40:04.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The Department is also implementing innovative programs implemented under the President's

asr-000539
00:40:04.840 --> 00:40:10.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Administration designed to address specific dimensions of poverty and vulnerability.

asr-000540
00:40:10.140 --> 00:40:14.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These are the Walang Gutom 2027 Program, the Tarabasa Tutoring Program, and the Pag-Abot

asr-000541
00:40:14.740 --> 00:40:15.740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Program.

asr-000542
00:40:15.740 --> 00:40:19.180
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: While each addresses a different dimension of poverty and vulnerability, they share a

asr-000543
00:40:19.180 --> 00:40:20.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: common objective.

asr-000544
00:40:20.260 --> 00:40:25.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Providing more responsive and innovative innovations to address the specific needs

asr-000545
00:40:25.260 --> 00:40:30.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: of vulnerable Filipinos and helping them move forward more sustainable and dignified lives.

asr-000546
00:40:30.380 --> 00:40:34.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Each program addresses a different challenge, but are all consistent with our broader objective

asr-000547
00:40:34.540 --> 00:40:39.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: of investing in human capacities, improving the circumstances of vulnerable Filipinos.

asr-000548
00:40:39.600 --> 00:40:43.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Let me now briefly discuss each flagship program stating with the Walang Gutom Program.

asr-000549
00:40:43.760 --> 00:40:48.400
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The Walang Gutom Program is the Department's flagship intervention to address food insecurity

asr-000550
00:40:48.400 --> 00:40:50.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: by providing targeted food assistance to poor

asr-000551
00:40:50.200 --> 00:40:52.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: households. For 2025,

asr-000552
00:40:52.760 --> 00:40:53.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the program

asr-000553
00:40:53.760 --> 00:40:54.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: provided food transfers

asr-000554
00:40:54.760 --> 00:40:55.760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to 300,000

asr-000555
00:40:55.760 --> 00:40:58.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: poor households. In 2026,

asr-000556
00:40:58.260 --> 00:41:04.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: implementation is being expanded to reach 750,000 food-insecure households by

asr-000557
00:41:04.580 --> 00:41:05.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the end of this year.

asr-000558
00:41:05.920 --> 00:41:11.780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For fiscal year 2027, 1.89 billion of this locally funded project with a physical target

asr-000559
00:41:11.780 --> 00:41:17.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: of 50,000 is allocated and 3.87 billion of foreign assisted project of refuel with a

asr-000560
00:41:17.720 --> 00:41:19.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: physical target of 750,000

asr-000562
00:41:20.200 --> 00:41:23.520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: effectively expanding the program's coverage.

asr-000563
00:41:23.520 --> 00:41:26.180
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The Tarabasa Tutoring Program addresses learning gaps

asr-000564
00:41:26.180 --> 00:41:28.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: among children while providing opportunities

asr-000565
00:41:28.220 --> 00:41:31.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: for young people to participate as youth tutors

asr-000566
00:41:31.560 --> 00:41:33.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and youth development workers.

asr-000567
00:41:33.640 --> 00:41:35.940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It is designed as a two-way intervention,

asr-000568
00:41:35.940 --> 00:41:38.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: supporting learners while they also provide

asr-000569
00:41:38.420 --> 00:41:41.240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: meaningful engagement and assistance to the youth

asr-000570
00:41:41.240 --> 00:41:43.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and the parents or guardians of the learners.

asr-000571
00:41:43.860 --> 00:41:45.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: As part of further clarifying

asr-000572
00:41:45.380 --> 00:41:47.440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the program's core intervention,

asr-000573
00:41:47.440 --> 00:41:49.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we are also proposing to rename the program

asr-000574
00:41:49.620 --> 00:41:52.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: as the Tarabasa Cash for Work Program

asr-000575
00:41:52.200 --> 00:41:54.440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to more clearly reflect its primary mechanism

asr-000576
00:41:54.440 --> 00:41:56.720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: of providing cash for work opportunities

asr-000577
00:41:56.720 --> 00:41:59.440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to the youth while delivering tutorial support

asr-000578
00:41:59.440 --> 00:42:02.620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to learners and participation incentive

asr-000579
00:42:02.620 --> 00:42:04.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to parents or guardians.

asr-000580
00:42:04.160 --> 00:42:05.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The program has demonstrated

asr-000581
00:42:05.500 --> 00:42:08.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: strong implementation performance in 2025

asr-000582
00:42:08.640 --> 00:42:11.940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and is on its path to reaching its targets for 2026.

asr-000583
00:42:11.940 --> 00:42:14.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For 2027, we are proposing 900 million

asr-000584
00:42:14.920 --> 00:42:18.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to support 66,633 beneficiaries,

asr-000585
00:42:18.340 --> 00:42:19.600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: including 47,595

asr-000586
00:42:19.600 --> 00:42:21.840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: learners.

asr-000587
00:42:21.840 --> 00:42:24.440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This investment will allow us to sustain the program

asr-000588
00:42:24.440 --> 00:42:26.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and continue addressing learning gaps

asr-000589
00:42:26.220 --> 00:42:27.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: while creating opportunities

asr-000590
00:42:27.920 --> 00:42:29.860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: for youth participation and development.

asr-000591
00:42:30.960 --> 00:42:33.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The Pag-Abot Program aims to reach out

asr-000592
00:42:33.160 --> 00:42:35.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to vulnerable and disadvantaged children,

asr-000593
00:42:35.020 --> 00:42:37.700
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: individuals, and families in street situations

asr-000594
00:42:37.700 --> 00:42:40.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and providing them with access to social protection services

asr-000595
00:42:40.800 --> 00:42:43.480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and appropriate interventions based on their needs.

asr-000596
00:42:43.480 --> 00:42:46.140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: As part of the integrated response,

asr-000597
00:42:46.140 --> 00:42:48.420
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: the program also implements the Walang Gutom Kitchen,

asr-000598
00:42:48.420 --> 00:42:50.500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: which gives immediate food assistance

asr-000599
00:42:50.500 --> 00:42:52.260
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: while connecting them to other appropriate

asr-000600
00:42:52.260 --> 00:42:54.540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: social welfare services.

asr-000601
00:42:54.540 --> 00:42:58.120
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The program has demonstrated strong implementation performance,

asr-000602
00:42:58.120 --> 00:43:01.100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: reaching 99.48% fund

asr-000603
00:43:01.100 --> 00:43:04.200
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: utilization in 2025,

asr-000604
00:43:04.200 --> 00:43:07.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with 6,846 clients served,

asr-000605
00:43:07.160 --> 00:43:11.160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: while in 2026, the program has served more than 10,000 clients

asr-000606
00:43:11.160 --> 00:43:16.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with a 63.71 utilization of its 807 million budget.

asr-000607
00:43:16.560 --> 00:43:18.960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For fiscal year 2027, we are proposing 807 million to provide,

asr-000608
00:43:18.960 --> 00:43:24.240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: provide assistance to 5,000 clients. Through Pagabot, we are bringing social protection closer

asr-000609
00:43:24.240 --> 00:43:29.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to vulnerable and disadvantaged families, individuals, and families in street situation

asr-000610
00:43:29.340 --> 00:43:34.440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: who may otherwise remain outside the reach of regular government intervention. Beyond our major

asr-000611
00:43:34.440 --> 00:43:40.640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: programs, the SWD is also developing responses to prevent emerging social welfare needs.

asr-000612
00:43:40.840 --> 00:43:46.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These include initiatives such as Project Aruga, ProtecTEEN, Project SAFE for OSAEC victims,

asr-000613
00:43:46.580 --> 00:43:51.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: which also addresses specific vulnerabilities and emerging concerns among children,

asr-000614
00:43:51.580 --> 00:43:56.020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: adolescents, and family. This initiative demonstrates our continuing effort to make

asr-000615
00:43:56.020 --> 00:44:01.080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: social protection more responsive to changing needs and emerging vulnerabilities.

asr-000616
00:44:02.640 --> 00:44:07.800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The DSWD social protection and social welfare mandate is complemented by the work for

asr-000617
00:44:07.800 --> 00:44:13.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: attached and supervised agencies. Should this body wish for us to proceed, I can present in

asr-000618
00:44:13.380 --> 00:44:15.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: brief the financial performance of each agency,

asr-000619
00:44:16.260 --> 00:44:16.560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: or I can present the financial performance of each agency,

asr-000620
00:44:16.560 --> 00:44:19.580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: or I can call the heads of the ASAS to present and answer questions,

asr-000621
00:44:19.860 --> 00:44:22.920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: should you have any, on the performance of their agencies.

asr-000622
00:44:28.400 --> 00:44:37.220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, I think I've read the whole NEP summary, so I will now have to close.

asr-000623
00:44:37.420 --> 00:44:40.900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We thank the honorable members of the committee and your continued support for the department

asr-000624
00:44:40.900 --> 00:44:45.340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and our shared commitment to empower people and communities and improve the lives of our

asr-000625
00:44:45.340 --> 00:44:45.940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: fellow Filipinos.

asr-000626
00:44:45.940 --> 00:44:47.180
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-000627
00:44:47.960 --> 00:44:49.580
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Thank you, Mr. Secretary.

asr-000628
00:44:51.280 --> 00:44:58.080
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Before we move on to interpellations, may I remind our distinguished colleagues that each member is

asr-000629
00:44:58.080 --> 00:44:59.820
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: allotted 5 minutes

asr-000630
00:45:00.020 --> 00:45:07.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: for questions or interpellation excluding the responses of the resource persons.

asr-000631
00:45:07.020 --> 00:45:14.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: When the bell sounds, the member has 30 seconds to conclude.

asr-000632
00:45:14.020 --> 00:45:18.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Assistent with the longstanding practice of the house,

asr-000633
00:45:18.020 --> 00:45:24.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: the chair shall recognize minority, independent and majority members

asr-000634
00:45:24.020 --> 00:45:28.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: in an alternating manner when practicable.

asr-000635
00:45:28.020 --> 00:45:34.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: The chair first recognizes honorable uh

asr-000636
00:45:34.020 --> 00:45:42.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: before we move on, may I recognize first our members who just came in.

asr-000637
00:45:42.020 --> 00:45:47.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: We have vice chair Kit Mik Attorney Mike Tan,

asr-000638
00:45:47.020 --> 00:45:53.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Assistant Majority Leader Johan Monic Bautista

asr-000639
00:45:53.020 --> 00:45:57.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Representative Ferdinand B1 Beltran,

asr-000640
00:45:57.020 --> 00:46:02.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Representative John Attorney JP Padernos,

asr-000641
00:46:02.020 --> 00:46:09.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: Vice Chair Romel Rico Angara, Vice Chair Jerry Boy Espina

asr-000642
00:46:09.020 --> 00:46:13.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: and Representative Yolio Rodriguez.

asr-000643
00:46:13.020 --> 00:46:18.020
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: So for the first member who will be interpelating,

asr-000644
00:46:18.020 --> 00:46:26.360
Rep. JC Rahman A. Nava, M.D.: may we call on Representative Perci Cendaña.

asr-000645
00:46:26.360 --> 00:46:27.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Magandang umaga,

asr-000646
00:46:27.360 --> 00:46:28.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Mr. Chair at magandang

asr-000647
00:46:28.360 --> 00:46:32.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: umaga po sa DSWD family.

asr-000648
00:46:32.360 --> 00:46:40.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: According to the NCDA, there are 2.8 million Filipinos registered as PWDs.

asr-000649
00:46:40.360 --> 00:46:45.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kaya nakapagtataka po na nangalahati ang budget ng NCDA

asr-000650
00:46:45.360 --> 00:46:55.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: from 187 million in the 2026 GAA to a mere 91 million in the 2027 NEP.

asr-000651
00:46:55.360 --> 00:46:57.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: If we're going to do the math, that's

asr-000652
00:46:57.360 --> 00:47:01.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: only Php32 per PWD. Inuulit ko

asr-000653
00:47:01.360 --> 00:47:06.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: po, ang investment ng gobyerno sa darating na 2027, kung

asr-000654
00:47:06.360 --> 00:47:08.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: ang basihan po ay NEP,

asr-000655
00:47:08.360 --> 00:47:12.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: is only ₱32 per PWD.

asr-000656
00:47:12.360 --> 00:47:14.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ang tanong po ng marami, bakit

asr-000657
00:47:14.360 --> 00:47:18.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: parang discounted ang budget para sa PWD?

asr-000658
00:47:18.360 --> 00:47:24.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ano po ba ang dahilan at ah nabawasan na ganito kalaki ang budget ng ating NCDA?

asr-000659
00:47:24.360 --> 00:47:25.360
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Mr. Chair,

asr-000660
00:47:25.360 --> 00:47:28.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chair, una po sa lahat,

asr-000661
00:47:28.360 --> 00:47:33.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: syempre gusto ho namin na sana maibalik yung nawalang budget sa NCDA

asr-000662
00:47:33.360 --> 00:47:35.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: which is an attach agency. Pero

asr-000663
00:47:35.360 --> 00:47:39.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: gusto ko lang pong linawin na hindi naman ho ibig sabihin na nabawasan ang tulong at suporta ng

asr-000664
00:47:39.360 --> 00:47:41.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: pamalaan sa ating mga may Kapansanan.

asr-000665
00:47:41.360 --> 00:47:45.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Sa katunayan, malaking bahagi ho ng budget ng mother department

asr-000666
00:47:45.360 --> 00:47:50.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: itself goes through financial assistance through the program for people with disability.

asr-000667
00:47:50.360 --> 00:47:54.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yung mga innovation programs namin, yung mga bagong programa katulad ng Project

asr-000668
00:47:54.360 --> 00:47:59.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Aruga are also geared towards people with disabilities and their families.

asr-000669
00:47:59.360 --> 00:48:02.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So we will provide the committee a disaggregated

asr-000670
00:48:02.360 --> 00:48:05.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: data based on the mother department spending on people with disability.

asr-000671
00:48:05.360 --> 00:48:09.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So we would like to assure the good representation na hindi ho nababawasan.

asr-000672
00:48:09.360 --> 00:48:12.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ngayon ho pag titignan natin yung mandate kasi ng

asr-000673
00:48:12.360 --> 00:48:14.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: NCDA they were really tasked to

asr-000674
00:48:14.360 --> 00:48:17.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: one do policies for people with disabilities

asr-000675
00:48:17.360 --> 00:48:20.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: to to capacitate local government units kasi

asr-000676
00:48:20.360 --> 00:48:23.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: devolved po. LGUs have PDAO offices

asr-000677
00:48:23.360 --> 00:48:26.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: or people with the disability affairs offices.

asr-000678
00:48:26.360 --> 00:48:28.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yun ho yung mga implementing arm.

asr-000679
00:48:28.360 --> 00:48:30.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So yung mga budget n nakabukod

asr-000680
00:48:30.360 --> 00:48:33.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: now itong nawalang budget na to ay capital expenditure.

asr-000681
00:48:33.360 --> 00:48:38.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Nakalagay po iyan sa libro ng NCDA to provide IT equipment to the different PDAO

asr-000682
00:48:38.360 --> 00:48:42.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: offices. Kasi alam natin may mga PDAO offices na maliliit ang LGU

asr-000683
00:48:42.360 --> 00:48:45.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: at walang kapasidad na mag bumili ng kanilang mga gamit.

asr-000684
00:48:45.360 --> 00:48:48.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So yun ho yung na walang suporta kasi non-recurring

asr-000685
00:48:48.360 --> 00:48:51.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: po siya. Pero pagdating ho naman sa direct grants and subsidies,

asr-000686
00:48:51.360 --> 00:48:52.360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: wala

