05:07:03.840 --> 05:07:07.800
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: Good afternoon, my colleagues, most especially good afternoon to the whole DSWD family.

asr-006524
05:07:07.800 --> 05:07:09.800
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: Secretary, good afternoon.

asr-006525
05:07:09.800 --> 05:07:12.800
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: This is quite short, just a manifestation.

asr-006526
05:07:12.800 --> 05:07:16.380
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: Our district is heavily ravaged by Typhoon Tino.

asr-006527
05:07:16.380 --> 05:07:18.380
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: I think many of you were there.

asr-006528
05:07:18.380 --> 05:07:24.380
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: We had a number of hanging bridges then built under the Kalahi Seeds program.

asr-006529
05:07:24.380 --> 05:07:28.380
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: I think almost all were destroyed during the Typhoon Tino.

asr-006530
05:07:28.380 --> 05:07:32.260
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: So maybe you can take a look at those hanging bridges.

asr-006531
05:07:32.260 --> 05:07:37.920
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: But more importantly, we'd just like to thank you and commend the DSWD.

asr-006532
05:07:38.580 --> 05:07:52.920
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: Our district was not only ravaged by Typhoon Tino, we have underwent maybe four or five eruptions of Mount Kanlaon and just recently the devastation of the sugar industry with the red-striped soft scale insect.

asr-006533
05:07:53.220 --> 05:07:56.880
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: In all of this, I think our able partner has been the DSWD.

asr-006534
05:07:56.880 --> 05:07:58.080
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: So thank you.

asr-006535
05:07:58.380 --> 05:08:07.380
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: Secretary, the whole DSWD family, and a special commendation to our, I don't know if it's here, our regional director, Director Arwin.

asr-006536
05:08:07.380 --> 05:08:09.380
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: Thank you, regional director Arwin.

asr-006537
05:08:09.380 --> 05:08:10.380
Rep. Emilio Bernardino L. Yulo: Thank you, sir.

asr-006538
05:08:10.380 --> 05:08:12.380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Mr. Chair, we'll look into those Kalahi bridges.

